 ## Deadlines and filing
 
-**Who must file** ([§ 25(1) GewStDV](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/gewstdv_1955/__25.html)): every liable business whose trade income "den Betrag von 24 500 Euro überstiegen hat"; every non-exempt capital company and cooperative, whatever the amount; a business with a loss carry-forward determined at the end of the last period; any business the tax office asks. A sole trader at or below EUR 24,500 with no loss carry-forward and no request files nothing. Note the test is on trade income before rounding: EUR 24,580 rounds to EUR 24,500, gives no tax, yet a return is due.
+**Who must file** ([§ 25(1) GewStDV](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/gewstdv_1955/__25.html)): every liable business whose trade income "den Betrag von 24 500 Euro überstiegen hat"; every non-exempt capital company, cooperative and insurance mutual association, whatever the amount; other private-law legal persons and associations without legal personality, insofar as they have a commercial operation other than agriculture/forestry whose trade income exceeds EUR 5,000; standing commercial businesses of public-law legal persons whose trade income exceeds EUR 5,000; and the partly exempt businesses listed in § 25(1) no. 5 GewStDV only where they also carry on a taxable activity and taxable trade income exceeds EUR 5,000. The separate overrides remain: a business with a loss carry-forward determined at the end of the last period; any business the tax office asks. A sole trader at or below EUR 24,500 with no loss carry-forward and no request files nothing. Note the test is on trade income before rounding: EUR 24,580 rounds to EUR 24,500, gives no tax, yet a return is due.
 
 **What.** A declaration for setting the base amount and, where § 28 applies, an apportionment declaration, sent electronically in the official data format. On request the tax office can accept a signed paper form to avoid undue hardship ([§ 14a GewStG](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/gewstg/__14a.html)).
 
